// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 7 „Haridus ja õppimine” (b1b2-031…035), stage B2-.
// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline in January–February, a year after the B1
// course: Mia is in class 1 and gets her first verbal half-year report, Oskar (class 4.b, teacher Kristel Saar) has
// falling maths grades and has to choose between football four times a week and the school's robotics club (leader
// Kuldar), Sofia prepares for her B2 exam in March at Keelekool Sõna (teacher Maret) and mentors the trainee Laura,
// Helgi looks back on 35 years of grades as a teacher; the education researcher Helen Rebane (module 5) writes an
// article and gives a lecture at Kase kool. One goal said on the first sheet: at the end the learner takes part in the
// Kase kool board meeting (hoolekogu, chair Marje Lepp) on verbal feedback instead of grades in classes 4–6 (Harno B2
// debate with pro / contra cards → a decision) and writes a summary with a comment (~180 words) for the school
// newsletter „Kase kooli infoleht” (034 Kasuta).
// Grammar (B2, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md §5), spiral: government of verbs and adjectives in education texts —
// huvituma millest, keskenduma millele, harjuma millega, osalema milles, uhke mille üle, mures mille pärast (031, back
// in 033 and in the 034 error correction); nominal style preview -mine / -ja — õppimine, hindamine, sõnade kordamine,
// õppija (032, used in the 034 proposal; taught fully in module 12); the quotative and source phrases in reporting
// research — uuringu järgi, Rebase sõnul, väidetakse, tagasiside olevat… (033, back in 034). Module 6's work words
// return: juht, töökoormus, tagasiside, ületunnid, arenguvestlus, vastutus, meeskond, kolleeg, graafik, juhatus,
// küsitlus, eelis, puudus, and its essive (töötab õpetajana, osaleb esindajana).
// Harno B2 formats trained: lecture gap fill (033), 4-option cloze (032), sentence bank (033), article with an analysis
// (033), semi-formal letter ~140 words (031, 032), 1-min monologue on a work topic (031, 034), debate with argument
// cards and a decision, summary with a comment ~180 words (034).
//   031 Mia's verbal report and arenguvestlus (listening), the newsletter on what keeps the wish to learn; Oskar's
//       arenguvestlus with Kristel Saar — football or robotics, an agreement in a letter.
//   032 Sofia's call with Helgi on study methods (listening), Maret's guide (cloze); Sofia mentors Laura before her
//       logistics exam — a talk at lunch and a study plan in a letter.
//   033 Helen Rebane's article on grades (analysis), her lecture at Kase kool (lecture gap fill), Helgi's 35 years of
//       grades (sentence bank); Jaan sums the lecture up for Kadri and for the 4.b parents' chat.
//   034 The parents' proposal to the board (survey chart, the four parts of a proposal), a robotics-club proposal, the
//       learner's own proposal; the board meeting with argument cards and the summary with a comment for the newsletter.
// Lesson 5 (035) is the module's check in Harno B2 form (unchanged). The v3 file is in archive/v3/b2/module07.js.
